Why: Pyodide has no pthreads (single-threaded wasm). emcc accepts -pthread, so dependency('threads')
succeeds and pixman-1.pc then carries `-pthread -sPTHREAD_POOL_SIZE=4` into every consumer, producing
shared-memory wasm that cannot be linked into a Pyodide side module. Treat emscripten as having no threads.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -464,7 +464,13 @@
   config.set('HAVE_LIBPNG', 1)
 endif
 dep_m = cc.find_library('m', required : false)
-dep_threads = dependency('threads')
+# Pyodide is single-threaded: emcc accepts -pthread and dependency('threads') would add it (plus
+# -sPTHREAD_POOL_SIZE) to pixman-1.pc, shared-memory-izing everything that links pixman.
+if host_machine.system() == 'emscripten'
+  dep_threads = null_dep
+else
+  dep_threads = dependency('threads')
+endif
 
 # MSVC-style compilers do not come with pthreads, so we must link
 # to it explicitly, currently pthreads-win32 is supported
